IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `gdpr-core`
IMPORT `gdpr-core-2`
IMPORT `gdpr-definitions-2`
IMPORT `P2-art-13`
IMPORT `P2-art-14`
IMPORT `P2-seat-subject`
IMPORT `P2-seat-controller`

-- tests-independent-2-items.l4: a second round by the independent test author.
-- It asserts, from lead/answers.md only, the blocks that tests-independent-2.l4 listed as "no function asks this" and that the seat questions added after the first review now ask.
-- Every expected value is the one in answers.md for the block named in the comment above the assertion, written before this file was run.
-- A block that a seat question still does not ask is a comment line "-- <id>: still no function asks this (<why>)".


-- C3-001: still no function asks this (the seat asks whether the controller has taken the measures, not whether it must)
-- C3-002: still no function asks this (the seat asks whether the information given is concise and plain, not whether the data subject is entitled to it)
-- C3-005: still no function asks this (the seat asks whether the controller has facilitated the exercise, not whether it must)
-- C3-015: still no function asks this (the new months question for the notice of extension takes no inputs, so it cannot carry the block's fact that the extension was not necessary; the clock still takes "has been extended" as a plain fact)
-- C3-016: still no function asks this (the clock function has no input for whether the message is a request under Articles 15 to 22)
-- C3-020: still no function asks this (the seat asks whether the information has been provided by electronic means, and has a "provided" input; no function asks whether the data subject is entitled to it)
-- C3-021: still no function asks this (same: the seat takes "the information is provided by electronic means" as an input)
-- C3-027: still no function asks this (the new Article 12(4) question for the data subject asks how many months the controller has (a NUMBER); no yes/no question asks whether the data subject is entitled to be told the reasons and the complaint and remedy)
-- C3-028: still no function asks this (the seat asks whether the information was provided free of charge (a fee input), not whether the data subject is entitled to it)
-- C3-033: still no function asks this (the seat asks whether the controller has borne the burden (compliance), not whether it must)
-- C3-034: still no function asks this (no seat question asks whether the data subject bears a burden)
-- C3-037: still no function asks this (the one input bundles "reasonable doubts" with "the request referred to in Articles 15 to 21"; no input says the request is under Article 22)
-- C3-040: still no function asks this (the seat asks whether the icons I present are machine-readable (a "machine-readable" input), not whether they must be)
-- C3-041: still no function asks this (no function asks about the language of the information)
-- C3-042
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller` FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- C3-043
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a data subject, where the controller collected my personal data from me, am I entitled to be given the item of information I name` TRUE `Art 13(1)(b) the contact details of the data protection officer` FALSE TRUE `P2 subject answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- C3-044
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(1)(b) the contact details of the data protection officer` FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- C3-045
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(1)(d) the legitimate interests pursued by the controller or by a third party` FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: yes` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- C3-046
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(1)(e) the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data` FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- C3-047
-- note: the seat input is "intends to transfer"; the block's fact that the transfer is one referred to in Article 46 has no input of its own
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(1)(f) the intended transfer to a third country or international organisation and the adequacy decision or the safeguards` FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- C3-048: still no function asks this (the Article 13(1) item question takes no input saying which subparagraph of Article 49(1) a transfer relies on; the safeguards reference is part of item (f) as a whole)
-- C3-049
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(2)(c) the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- C3-050
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(2)(c) the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing before its withdrawal` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- C3-051
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of further information he or she names` TRUE `Art 13(2)(f) the existence of automated decision-making, including profiling, and meaningful information about the logic involved, the significance and the envisaged consequences` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- C3-052: OPEN reading, moved to tests-independent-2-open.l4 (lead triage 2026-11-26): Art 13(2)(f) "at least in those cases"; the encoding takes F13-3 reading A (JUST FALSE: the item is not required outside the named cases), the author reads "list not closed": NOTHING
-- C3-053
-- note: the block says all the required information was given on the day of obtaining; the seat "includes" inputs are TRUE for the items that apply (identity, purposes, legal basis) and FALSE for items that do not (no representative, no DPO, no legitimate-interest basis, no recipients, no transfer)
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, have I provided, at the time I obtain them, all of the information that paragraph 1 lists` TRUE FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is met`
-- C3-054
-- note: as C3-053 with the information given a day after obtaining: "provided at the time" is FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, have I provided, at the time I obtain them, all of the information that paragraph 1 lists` TRUE FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
-- C3-055
-- note: translation: the function asks "have I provided" and answers a Duty outcome; the block's "no duty here" is the duty not arising (not a new question: it was open to me before and I skipped it)
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(1), as a controller, where I collect personal data from the data subject, have I provided, at the time I obtain them, all of the information that paragraph 1 lists` FALSE FALSE FALSE `P2 controller answer: no` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the duty does not arise`
-- C3-060
-- note: the per-item input "the data subject already has the item" is FALSE for the storage period; what the data subject already has (identity, contact details) is not an input of this question
#ASSERT `Under Article 13(2), as a data subject, where the controller collected my personal data from me, am I entitled to be given the item of further information I name` TRUE `Art 13(2)(a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or the criteria used to determine that period` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- C3-061: still no function asks this (the item choice lists only what Article 13(1) lists; it has no member for the categories of personal data, so the question cannot be put)
-- C3-062
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(1), as a controller, where I have not obtained the personal data from the data subject, must I give the data subject the item of information he or she names` TRUE `P2 controller answer: no` `Art 14(1)(a) the identity and the contact details of the controller` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- C3-063
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(1), as a data subject, where the controller did not obtain my personal data from me, am I entitled to be given the item of information I name` TRUE `P2 subject answer: no` `Art 14(1)(d) the categories of personal data concerned` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- C3-064
#ASSERT `Under Article 14(2), as a data subject, where the controller did not obtain my personal data from me, am I entitled to be given the item of further information I name` TRUE `P2 subject answer: no` `P2 subject answer: no` `Art 14(2)(f) the source from which the personal data originate and, if applicable, whether it came from publicly accessible sources` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- C3-072: still no function asks this (the Article 14(3) functions have no input for whether the data were obtained from the data subject)
-- C3-075: still no function asks this (the Article 14(5)(b) question still asks whether the controller has taken the measures (compliance), not whether it must)
-- C3-078: still no function asks this (the item choice lists only what Article 14(1) and (2) list; it has no member for a right to compensation)
-- C3-088: still no function asks this (the seat input is "transferred to a third country"; none says the transfer relies on Article 49 and not Article 46)
-- C3-089: still no function asks this (the seat asks whether the controller has provided a copy (compliance), not whether it must)
-- C3-092: still no function asks this (the seat asks whether the information has been provided in electronic form (a "provided" input), not whether the data subject is entitled to it)
-- C3-093: still no function asks this (same: the seat takes "the information is provided in a commonly used electronic form" as an input)
-- C3-095: still no function asks this (no function asks about an item that Article 15(1) does not list)
-- C3-100: still no function asks this (no function asks whether a delay in days is undue)
-- C3-112: still no function asks this (unchanged: the Article 17(2) question asks whether the controller has taken reasonable steps)
-- C3-113: still no function asks this (the seat asks whether the controller has taken reasonable steps (compliance), not whether it must)
-- C3-121: still no function asks this (no input says whose personal data the erasure concerns)
-- C3-133: still no function asks this (no function asks whether Article 18 gives a right to rectification)
-- C3-134: still no function asks this (the seat asks whether the controller has communicated the change (compliance), not whether it must)
-- C3-136: still no function asks this (the seat asks whether the controller has informed the data subject (compliance), not whether the data subject is entitled)
-- C3-170: still no function asks this (the seat asks whether the controller has implemented the measures (compliance), not whether it must)
-- C3-172: still no function asks this (no function asks about a measure beyond the three named)
-- C3-179: still no function asks this (no function asks how far a valid restriction reaches (the extent is set by the restricting law, outside the text))
-- C3-180: still no function asks this (the seat asks whether the measure contains the provisions (compliance), not whether it must)
-- C3-181: still no function asks this (the seat asks whether the measure contains the provisions (compliance), not whether it must)
